{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Coordination note for epic eb64 (runner/reconciler/operation-boundary convergence)\n\n**Timing:** the eb64 conflict-avoidance guidance reached me *after* this fix had already landed\nand this ticket was closed, so I could not hold it for sequencing. Recording exactly what is now\non `main` so eb64 can rebase onto it and preserve the invariant rather than re-introduce the gap.\n\n**Landed commit:** `44e34af1065d3e084e73a58c223a9fd7a0e44783` on `origin/main`\n(\"Record LLM spend when finalize_outcome raises\", `rebar-ticket: fe75-a4a3-9eef-457c`,\nChange-Id `Ic904f7a80d969596e8543a91ca8c641c504b7023`, Gerrit change 2417, LLM-Review +1 /\nVerified +1). Gerrit's Rebase-If-Necessary submit rebased my patch cleanly onto latest main.\n\n**Single-file blast radius (in eb64's declared `src/rebar/llm/` territory):**\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` — `PydanticAIRunner.run()` finalization tail, ~lines 728–767.\n  The ONLY structural change: `finalize_outcome(...)` + the success-only tail\n  (`result[\"_usage\"] = usage`, `_merge_success_run_shape(...)`) are now inside a `try:`, and the\n  pre-existing final `record_call_spend(...)` moved into a `finally:`. No lines added/removed\n  elsewhere; success path is byte-identical (finally fires last, after the shape merge).\n- `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py` — the c465 characterization test renamed to\n  `test_a_raise_in_finalize_outcome_still_logs_and_records_the_spend_row`, asserting the fixed\n  behavior.\n\n**Invariant eb64 MUST preserve through any runner-lifecycle refactor:** when `finalize_outcome`\n(or any post-model finalization step) raises after the model call has consumed tokens,\n`record_call_spend` still runs exactly once for that call before the exception propagates, and\nthe original exception's disposition is unchanged. The regression test above is the guard — keep\nit green. Did NOT touch `failure.py` / `_errors.py` / `gate_dispatch.py` (error-code epic 3405's\nterritory).\n\nIf eb64 is rewriting `run()`'s finalization such that a straight rebase is non-trivial, treat\nthis as the source-of-truth for the required behavior; ping me if you'd like me to re-apply the\nordering on top of the refactored shape."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788073024513039316,"uuid":"7049cf04-fd9d-47bf-a76d-a6c049a6a1ff"}